# Shell scripts MUST be checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Added 2026-08-27 after scripts/generate-api-types.sh shipped to main unable to
# run: it was written on the Windows side of a WSL2 mount, got CRLF, and bash
# read the shebang as `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` and `set -euo pipefail\r` — which
# fails with `set: pipefail: invalid option name`. The script's own test checked
# that the generated output existed, not that the script executed, so nothing
# caught it.
#
# Deliberately narrow. This repo has long-standing CRLF drift across ~60 files
# and a blanket `* text=auto` would renormalise all of them in one unreviewable
# commit. Shell scripts are the case where the line ending decides whether the
# file *works*, so they are the case worth fixing now.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are executed or pasted somewhere that cares.
*.bash text eol=lf
